\ scimark SOR (successive over-relaxation), N=100 — port of pyperformance
\ bm_scimark's SOR kernel. G is a flat row-major double-segment (idx = y·N + x,
\ exactly Array2D's layout); the stencil updates each interior cell in place.
\
\ G is allocated per outer iteration and left all-zero, as bench_SOR does, so
\ this measures loop throughput and the checksum is 0; the stencil arithmetic on
\ seeded data is checked by tests/152_scimark_kernels.h2o. Outer repeat count
\ comes from iterations; the inner relaxation runs cycles sweeps, as in the
\ reference (cycles = 10).

100 to iterations

variable g
100.0 constant n
99.0 constant nm1
10000.0 constant nn
10.0 constant cycles
1.25 0.25 f* constant omega-over-four
1.0 1.25 f- constant one-minus-omega

: build-g ^g |
  nn double-segment to g ;

: sor-execute
  0.0 to cycle
  begin cycle cycles < while
     1.0 to y
     begin y nm1 < while
        y n f* to rowbase
        1.0 to x
        begin x nm1 < while
           rowbase x f+ to idx
           g idx n f- @i
           g idx n f+ @i f+
           g idx 1.0 f- @i f+
           g idx 1.0 f+ @i f+
           omega-over-four f*
           one-minus-omega  g idx @i f*  f+  to nv
           g idx nv !i drop
           x 1.0 f+ to x
        repeat
        y 1.0 f+ to y
     repeat
     f++ cycle
  repeat ;

: sor-checksum ( -- s )

  0.0
  [: g swap @i f+ :] nn i-times
  to total
  total ;

: sor-bench
  now to t0
  [: build-g sor-execute :] iterations times
  now t0 - to t0
  "elapsed: " . t0 . " s" . cr
  sor-checksum "checksum: {0}" format . cr ;

sor-bench
bye
